  "id": "humans",
  "lore": "*\"Everyone else was made for something. We just stayed.\"*\n\nHumans are most of the people in the Ninth World, and almost everyone in Wickhaven. They're the ones the prior worlds didn't bother to redesign: unspecialised, adaptable, and stubborn. They have no built-in gland, core or lineage, and that's their strength. Humans learn anything, live anywhere, and keep going after better-made peoples give up.\n\nHumans of the Ninth World aren't quite the humans of long ago, either. Ten thousand years of old-world leftovers have marked them in small ways. Many have a harmless **oddity of birth**: eyes of two colours, hair that changes shade with the seasons, skin that's warm to the touch in winter. These never affect the rules.",
