  "id": "lightborn",
  "lore": "*\"The midwife said I didn't cry. I just lay there and glowed.\"*\n\nThe Lightborn are humans born with **old light** in the blood: the same pale, living light that the Lanterns gather. Nobody chooses it and nobody can predict it. A Lightborn can be born to any human family, and it happens most often in the shadow of a lit Lantern. From birth there's a faint glow under the skin, like a candle behind paper, and the eyes are pale, almost white.\n\nMost Lightborn hear a **voice in the light** at some point in their childhood. It speaks in dreams or in moments of danger, and it gives advice, warnings, or sometimes nothing but a feeling. Some trust it completely. Others spend their lives trying to ignore it.",
