  "id": "ashmaw",
  "lore": "*\"Don't stand in front of me when I cough.\"*\n\nThe Ashmaw are tall, scaled people with long jaws, heavy tails and a hard ridge of plates along the skull. Deep in the throat, every Ashmaw has a **breath gland**: an organ that mixes and stores a fierce chemical and spits it out in a blast. The gland's chemistry decides the colour of their scales, and each family line has its own. A Copper Ashmaw breathes acid, a Red one fire, a Silver one a freezing mist.\n\nNobody knows who made them. The Ashmaw say they were made by nobody: that they are the old beasts of the Ninth World, the ones the prior worlds feared, who learned to walk and talk on their own. Scholars think it's more likely they were built. Ashmaw don't like scholars.",
