  "id": "stonebound",
  "lore": "*\"The sky is very nice. It's also very big, and there's nothing holding it up.\"*\n\nThe Stonebound are short, broad, heavy-boned people built for life underground. A prior world shaped them to live and work deep in the earth, in the shafts, vaults and machine-halls it left beneath the Ninth World. Their bones are dense as stone, their blood scrubs out bad air, their eyes see far in the dark, and their feet feel the rock: a Stonebound standing on stone can tell where people are walking a long way off.\n\nMany Stonebound still live in the deep places their ancestors were made for: old halls sealed behind iron doors, warm, lit and quiet. Others have come up to the surface to trade, dig or wander, and most of them never quite get used to the sky.",
