  "lore": "*\"It's not broken. It's thinking.\"*\n\nThe Tinkerfolk are a small, quick people, three to four feet tall, with big bright eyes, nimble fingers and minds that never stop. A prior world made them to work inside its machines: to crawl through ducts too narrow for anyone else, read old signals, and keep the great engines running. The engines are long dead, but the Tinkerfolk aren't. They still love tight spaces, odd noises and anything with moving parts.\n\nTheir minds were built to be hard to fool, and they are. A Tinkerfolk is very difficult to trick, frighten or bewilder, which makes them both good company and annoying to argue with.",
